Explanation

The 8-puzzle problem is a sliding puzzle where we arrange tiles to reach the goal state.

It uses A* algorithm, which is an informed search technique.
It finds the optimal (shortest) path to reach the goal.
Working
Start with an initial puzzle state.
Generate possible moves (up, down, left, right).
Use heuristic (Manhattan distance) to estimate cost.
Select the node with the lowest f(n) = g(n) + h(n):
g(n) → cost from start
h(n) → estimated cost to goal
Repeat until goal state is reached.
Functions Used
heuristic() → calculates Manhattan distance
get_neighbors() → generates next possible states
astar() → implements A* algorithm
print_state() → displays puzzle
